# OCULUM — Card creation checklist

Every time you add or regenerate a card, do this **before** shipping Codex entries or finished art.

## 0. Placeholders before GenerateImage (required)

**Do not GenerateImage full faces in the same pass as Wave defs/engine** unless the user explicitly asks for art now.

Order:

1. **Defs + engine + tests + docs** — cards live in `CARDS`; missing `public/assets/cards/{id}.jpg` is fine
2. Runtime uses **procedural placeholder faces** (`cardBake.ts` heresy colors + glyph) until art exists
3. **Art pass only after greenlight** — then GenerateImage finished 2:3 faces, **anatomy QA**, `install-card-faces.mjs`, cache bust

- **Do not** pass Motley/Ink finished card JPGs as GenerateImage `reference_image_paths` — motif bleed copies wrong craft chrome (masks/dice into Bellward, etc.). Use same-craft faces or `docs/ref/{craft}/` palette refs only.
- Figures must print `Veiled N / Witnessed M.` matching CardDef powers — never omit.
- Gender / cast mix (e.g. not Motley-stacking glamorous women; Bellward: 2 creature ♀ + 1 human ♀ modest + males) is locked in the placeholder / text pass, then honored in art prompts. Never default female Figures to exaggerated breasts.

Never leave a craft permanently on placeholders when the user has greenlit art — finished faces are still the end state.

## 0b. Anatomy QA — detect AI slop, then regenerate (required)

After every GenerateImage (and before `install-card-faces`), **Read the image** and inspect limbs/hands/faces. If any anomaly below is present, **do not install** — regenerate that id (retry until clean, or simplify pose: sleeves, mitts, hidden hands).

**Fail and regenerate on:**
- Extra arm / leg / hand / finger
- Arm or hand facing the wrong way (mirrored joint, thumb on wrong side of grip)
- Melted / fused / tangled fingers; claw-cluster hands; missing palm
- Impossible grip (rope/staff clipping through wrong anatomy)
- Disembodied or floating limb
- Wrist thinner than fingers / broken elbow silhouette
- Face-veil “holes” that accidentally show a second face when veil should be opaque

**Prefer on regenerate prompts:** long sleeves, cloth-wrapped mitt fists, one hand hidden, simple closed fist with correct thumb — less bare-finger detail.

This pass is mandatory for OCULUM card faces so we do not ship AI-slop limbs.

## 1. Read the set first

- Review existing cards in `src/core/cards.ts` and `docs/CARD_TEXT.md`
- Avoid duplicate roles (another cheap Cube seeker, another Ring Gaze clone, etc.) unless intentional upgrade/sidegrade
- Check schools, costs, and win paths (Break / Eclipse / Law) so the new card has a clear niche

## 2. Mechanics must match printed text

- `CardDef.text`, Codex copy, `docs/CARD_TEXT.md`, and (when art exists) baked art rules must say the **same** thing
- Wire the ability in `src/core/match.ts` (or confirm an existing generic path covers it)
- Stats on the face (Essence, Witness/Sight cost, power, Sight/turn) must match `CardDef` fields
- After wiring: add/adjust a focused test that asserts the printed effect

## 3. Art ↔ school ↔ role (after greenlight)

- Art subject must fit the **school** visual cues in `docs/ART_STYLE.md` (never copy reference sheets literally)
- Style refs include `docs/ref/` + `docs/ref/inspo-2026-08/` — remix mood/motifs only
- Silhouette/mood should read as the card’s job (Site landmark vs Figure vs Relic vs Rite)
- Full-face art stays **2:3**; export JPGs without cover-cropping into another ratio
- **Premium / future skins:** keep `premium: true` + optional `layers/{id}/` assets; presentation stays flat until `CARD_SKINS_ENABLED` is turned on
- **Never print “Rare”** on faces, Codex type lines, or docs headers — School · Type · cost only; `premium` is internal (sort pin / skins)

## 3b. How many special (premium) cards

Premiums are **mechanically top-level** pieces (unique win levers), not foil sidegrades. Keep the pool sparse:

| Pool size | Target premiums | Rough share |
|-----------|----------------:|------------:|
| ~25–30 (current) | **3** | ~10% |
| Soft launch ~45–60 | **4–6** | ~10% |
| 1.0 ~80–100 | **8–10** | ~10% |
| Large set later | stay near **~10%**, not a rare every wave |

Rules of thumb when adding cards:

- Waves of 6–8: **0–1 premium max** (do not dump 3 mythics in one wave again)
- **At most one premium per school** until the collectible pool is well past soft launch
- Prefer filling commons/uncommons that support schools over another mythic
- A new premium must beat or clearly outclass existing mid pieces in its niche (not a +1 body Abbess clone)
- If unsure whether a card is premium: **ship it without `premium: true`**

## 4. Fit the game (combos / curve / decks)

Ask before locking design:

- What existing cards does this **combo** with? (Gaze, grafts, Eclipse, Law schools, Stance, Vessels, Toll/Lure)
- Does it clog the curve or starve Sight/Essence?
- Is it buildable in a coherent deck theme (Cube veil, Hollow Gaze, Deal Eclipse, Ring steal, Bellward Toll, etc.)?
- Prefer effects that use keywords already in the rules (Revelation, Gaze, Blind, Graft, Stance, Eclipse, Toll, Lure, Resonance)

## 5. Definition of done

**Mechanics pass (placeholders OK):**
- [ ] In `CARDS` + Teach/Codex lists if collectible
- [ ] Engine behavior matches text
- [ ] Docs updated
- [ ] Tests cover the new effect
- [ ] No full-face assets yet → procedural placeholders

**Art pass (after user greenlight):**
- [ ] GenerateImage finished faces
- [ ] Anatomy QA passed (no extra/wrong limbs, no melted hands) — regenerate failures before install
- [ ] Installed under `public/assets/cards/` + cache bust
- [ ] Readable at hand size; printed bake text matches `CardDef` (including Veiled/Witnessed powers)
- [ ] Craft frame DNA correct (no Motley motif bleed onto other crafts)
